---
import BaseLayout from "../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
import HandDrawnRule from "../components/HandDrawnRule.astro";

const pageTitle = "Start Here | oobCREATIVE";
const description = "Start with the situation you recognize. oobCREATIVE helps you find a practical first move before choosing a service or AI tool.";
---

<BaseLayout title={pageTitle} description={description}>
  <section class="page-hero">
    <div class="site-shell page-hero__copy">
      <p class="eyebrow">Start here</p>
      <h1>You do not need to diagnose the service first.</h1>
      <p class="page-kicker">
        Start with the pressure you are actually feeling. The useful path usually becomes clearer once we separate the problem from the tool.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <HandDrawnRule />

  <section class="page-section">
    <div class="site-shell">
      <div class="choice-grid">
        <article class="choice-card">
          <p class="eyebrow">01 · Informed confidence</p>
          <h2>AI is available. We still do not know where it belongs.</h2>
          <p>
            You may already have subscriptions, experiments, or employees using AI on their own. The next useful step is not another demo. It is choosing a real workflow, defining what good looks like, and deciding what remains a human responsibility.
          </p>
          <a class="text-link" href="/services/communication-systems-ai/">See the practical AI path <span aria-hidden="true">→</span></a>
        </article>

        <article class="choice-card">
          <p class="eyebrow">02 · Shared capability</p>
          <h2>Too much still depends on people remembering how everything works.</h2>
          <p>
            The team may be capable, but decisions, context, standards, approvals, and communication keep returning to the same people. This is often a knowledge and workflow problem before it is an automation problem.
          </p>
          <a class="text-link" href="/services/communication-systems-ai/#knowledge">See communication and knowledge systems <span aria-hidden="true">→</span></a>
        </article>

        <article class="choice-card">
          <p class="eyebrow">03 · Clearer decisions</p>
          <h2>The work is valuable. People still have to work too hard to understand it.</h2>
          <p>
            When an offer, mission, website, or service has outgrown the way it is explained, more content rarely fixes the problem. Audience clarity, message structure, and a better decision path usually come first.
          </p>
          <a class="text-link" href="/services/">See the broader communication path <span aria-hidden="true">→</span></a>
        </article>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <HandDrawnRule />

  <section class="page-section">
    <div class="site-shell content-grid">
      <div class="content-grid__aside">
        <p class="eyebrow">A different situation?</p>
        <h2>Projects also stall, launches become complicated, and communication can turn reactive.</h2>
      </div>
      <div class="content-grid__main">
        <p class="section-copy">
          oobCREATIVE remains a full-service creative and communication partner. AI and systems are a strong current entry point because many teams are trying to make new technology useful without losing quality, trust, or human judgment. The larger work still includes positioning, websites, campaigns, storytelling, communication systems, and ongoing support.
        </p>
        <div class="action-row">
          <a class="button button--outline" href="/services/">See all service families</a>
          <a class="text-link" href="/work/">See work in context <span aria-hidden="true">→</span></a>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
